   "tag": "v0.15.0",
   "date": "2026-11-03",
   "page": "https://github.com/Xaxis/brickworks-releases/releases/tag/v0.15.0",
   "notes": "https://github.com/Xaxis/brickworks-releases/releases/tag/v0.15.0",
   "summary": "The desktop app is free, as brickworks.diy now says, and nothing in it asks about a plan. Instructions keeps the window moving while it works out a model's steps, where 0.14.0 held one frame there for a fifth to two fifths of a second. A click hinge turned on a slow or busy machine stops on a click short of what is in its way, where it could end inside its base. A model opened while the last was still being weighed shows its own weight. When Claude looks over a design, it hears when the model shows fewer colours than real sets of its theme. And in German, French and Spanish more of the Library's themes are named in the language.",
